-<aside id="patch-watch-hud" hidden style="position:fixed;left:8px;right:8px;top:60px;z-index:30;background:#102c30ee;padding:10px;border-radius:10px;max-width:520px;max-height:65vh;overflow:auto"><p id="patch-watch-readout" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><details id="patch-watch-colonies" hidden><summary>Individual colony changes</summary><p id="patch-watch-colony-readout" style="white-space:pre-line;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></p></details><button id="cancel-patch-watch">Stop / dismiss observation</button></aside><aside id="welcome-tip" hidden aria-label="Getting started"><p><b>Start a living planet.</b> Find water, seed simple aquatic life, then watch its descendants. World opens your saved planets; God tools are optional assistance. Pinch to zoom; drag to explore.</p><div class="tip-actions"><button id="start-guide">Show me how</button><button id="dismiss-guide">Not now</button></div></aside><dialog id="habitat-sheet" aria-labelledby="habitat-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="habitat-title">Preview habitat changes</h2><button id="habitat-close">Close / cancel</button></div><div class="sheet-actions"><button id="habitat-sunlit" style="min-height:44px">Preview Sunlit · 5 m shelf</button><button id="habitat-deep" style="min-height:44px">Preview Deep · 15 m shelf</button></div><p>Sunlit keeps the center and neighboring floor at 5 m for more light, with less stored water. Deep keeps a 5 m center and 15 m neighbors. Neither guarantees growth; seeding is a separate action.</p><p id="habitat-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="habitat-preview" hidden style="white-space:pre-line;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></p><p id="habitat-warning" hidden><strong>The rim will be raised and dried.</strong> Existing colonies on the rim may lose their habitat; floor colonies may also fare worse. This adds/removes water and changes terrain once, not life, nutrients or a permanent water supply.</p><button id="habitat-apply" hidden style="min-height:44px;width:100%">Apply this plan once</button><p id="habitat-receipt" hidden></p><p>Requires a paused Origin world. To pause, close this panel and use Play / Pause in the bottom dock, then request a fresh preview. Opening or closing this preview never pauses or resumes time.</p></dialog><dialog id="auto-seed-sheet" aria-labelledby="auto-seed-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="auto-seed-title">Auto-seed world</h2><button id="auto-seed-close">Close / cancel</button></div><p>Plan one seed at every eligible seed point on this planet at the moment the plan starts, including offscreen points. There is no visible-marker limit. This uses existing resources and free colony slots; it does not refill nutrients or water.</p><p id="auto-seed-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><button id="auto-seed-apply" hidden>Apply all planned seeds once</button><p>Requires paused Origin. Nothing changes until Apply. Cancel discards the plan. Seeding is a deliberate intervention, not natural birth or a guarantee of survival.</p></dialog><dialog id="more-menu" aria-labelledby="more-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="more-title">Planet tools</h2><button id="close-more" aria-label="Close planet tools">Close</button></div><nav hidden id="menu-groups" aria-label="Tool groups"><button id="menu-plant" aria-controls="group-plant" aria-pressed="true">Plant</button><button id="menu-observe" aria-controls="group-observe" aria-pressed="false">Observe</button><button id="menu-god" aria-controls="group-god" aria-pressed="false">God tools</button><button id="menu-world" aria-controls="group-world" aria-pressed="false">World</button><button id="menu-speed" aria-controls="group-speed" aria-pressed="false">Speed</button></nav><section id="group-plant" aria-label="Plant"><h3>Plant</h3><details id="origin-starter" hidden open><summary id="starter-summary">Start life · shape, seed, inspect</summary><div id="starter-actions"><button id="starter-find">Find habitat</button><button id="starter-basin" title="Shapes up to 19 patches: a 5 m nursery center and neighboring shelf, with a dry rim. Adds water once, not life.">Sunlit nursery</button><button id="starter-seed">Seed colony</button><button id="seed-targets-toggle" aria-pressed="true" title="Show or hide green planting circles and + targets only. Living colonies stay visible; arrival/loss effects have their own control.">Hide seed targets</button></div><p id="starter-info" role="status" aria-live="polite">Find habitat, optionally shape a shallow nursery, then Seed colony and Watch life. Nursery changes terrain and supplies water once, not life.</p></details><div id="origin-auto-seed" hidden><button id="auto-seed-open" disabled>Auto-seed world…</button><p>Review every currently eligible seed point before applying. Planning temporarily uses extra memory; save beforehand on large worlds. No ongoing automatic seeding.</p></div><section id="sandbox-defense-panel" hidden><h3>Inherited plant defenses</h3><button id="defense-land">Find land</button><p id="defense-policy">Optional: enable rare inherited defense variation in future offspring worldwide. Tough plants grow and spread slower and take longer to graze. Existing plants stay unchanged. Save first to restore the earlier rules.</p><button id="defense-enable">Enable inherited defenses</button><div id="defense-choices" hidden><button id="defense-tender">Plant tender</button><button id="defense-tough">Plant tough</button><button id="defense-cancel">Cancel planting</button><p>Tap an empty dry or shallow patch (up to 0.5 m water). Adds a founder with 35% cover; not natural evolution. Existing plants are retained. Toughness does not guarantee survival.</p></div><p id="defense-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></section><button id="help-toggle">Sandbox guide</button></section><section id="group-observe" aria-label="Observe" hidden><h3>Observe</h3><details id="world-ecology-panel" open><summary>Worldwide life · recent events</summary><button id="refresh-world-ecology">Refresh community sample</button><p id="world-ecology-readout" role="status" style="white-space:pre-line;overflow-wrap:anywhere">Open to sample current life and observed recent events.</p><div id="world-form-actions" aria-label="Visit a sampled living growth form"></div></details><div class="sheet-actions"><button id="find-life">Find existing life</button><button id="find-plants" hidden>Find plants</button><button id="find-rabbits" hidden>Find rabbits</button><button id="fit-life">Fit nearby life</button><button id="life-toggle">Life snapshot</button><button id="starter-watch">Watch life</button><button id="starter-inspect">Inspect</button><button id="arrival-effects-toggle" aria-pressed="true" title="Show or hide cyan arrival and amber tracked-loss effects. Does not hide living colonies or green seed hints, or stop event tracking.">Hide arrival/loss effects</button></div></section><section id="group-god" aria-label="God tools" hidden><h3>God tools</h3><p>Deliberate terrain, water, fire and colony interventions. Existing life can be harmed.</p><button id="god-toggle">Show God tools</button></section><section id="group-world" aria-label="World" hidden><h3>World</h3><button id="continue-world">Continue open world</button><p>New living planets include finite soil, wind dispersal and evolving cold/heat protection. Opening older saves keeps their original rules.</p><details id="world-library"><summary>Open a saved planet</summary><p>Start Play, then pause before opening a save. Starting the game does not save over your planet. Choose a save explicitly; originals remain unchanged. Multiple histories are never merged.</p><label for="world-library-source">Save history</label><select id="world-library-source"><option value="current">Saved planets</option><option value="main">Earlier main game</option><option value="wind">Earlier Wind worlds</option></select><button id="world-library-refresh">Find saved planets</button><label for="world-library-entry">Planet</label><select id="world-library-entry"></select><button id="world-library-import" disabled>Open selected planet…</button><button id="world-library-download" disabled>Download a copy</button><button id="world-library-cancel">Cancel selection</button><p id="world-library-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></details><details id="backup-recovery"><summary>Recovery backups</summary><p>Pause the world before restoring. Backups stay in this browser. Download a copy for safekeeping. Restore replaces only the open world after preserving it in a verified recovery checkpoint; the normal saved slot stays unchanged until you choose Save.</p><button id="recovery-refresh">Find saved backups</button><label for="recovery-backup">Verified backup</label><select id="recovery-backup"><option value="">Find backups first</option></select><button id="recovery-download" disabled>Download selected backup</button><button id="recovery-restore" disabled>Restore selected backup…</button><p id="recovery-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></details><button id="combined-new">Save + new living planet…</button><button id="combined-refresh">Refresh world details</button><p id="combined-status" role="status"></p><details id="combined-disclosure"><summary>How this world evolves</summary><p>New worlds begin with simple life. Roots, wind dispersal and cold/heat protection are inherited strategies with costs, not guaranteed land establishment. Evolving protection adds simulation work and may run slower. Older loaded worlds keep their saved rules.</p></details><div class="sheet-actions"><button id="save-world" disabled>Save planet</button><button id="load-world" disabled>Load planet</button><button id="land">Land</button><button id="fullscreen">Full screen</button></div><p>Save stays in this browser on this device. Before replacing an older save, this build preserves one exact pre-upgrade backup here. No cloud backup. Use Recovery backups in this panel to download or restore verified local checkpoints.</p></section><section id="group-speed" aria-label="Speed" hidden><h3>Speed</h3><p>Pause, requested speed, measured speed and bounded one-day advance.</p><button id="speed-toggle">Speed / fast-forward</button><button id="starter-speed">Fast-forward</button></section><p id="release-label">Stella Dei · evolving worlds</p></dialog><dialog id="speed-sheet" aria-labelledby="speed-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="speed-title">Simulation speed</h2><button id="close-speed">Close</button></div><p>Choose a target. Changing speed never unpauses your world.</p><div class="sheet-actions"><button id="speed-slow" aria-pressed="false">Slow · 1 hour / sec</button><button id="speed-grow" aria-pressed="false">Grow · 6 hours / sec</button><button id="speed-fast" aria-pressed="false">Fast-forward · 24 hours / sec</button></div><p id="speed-readout">Start a planet first.</p><p id="speed-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p>Target is your requested speed; Measured is what your device achieves. Simulation steps stay bounded. Time spent in the background is not caught up.</p><section aria-label="3D scene resolution"><h3>3D scene resolution</h3><div class="sheet-actions"><button id="scene-sharp" aria-pressed="false">Sharp · 100%</button><button id="scene-reduced" aria-pressed="false">Reduced · 75%</button><button id="scene-low" aria-pressed="false">Low · 50%</button></div><p id="scene-resolution-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p>Lower resolution makes the 3D planet softer and can reduce rendering work. Controls stay full resolution; simulation detail, time and saves are unchanged. Sharp is the default. This choice resets on page reload.</p></section><section><h3>Advance while paused · Origin</h3><button id="advance-day-start">Advance one day · hide globe</button><p>Pause your Origin world first. Runs 60 bounded simulation steps without drawing the globe between steps. This changes your world; Cancel keeps completed progress. Requested speed and saves are unchanged. No fixed completion time is promised.</p><p id="advance-day-error" role="status"></p></section><button id="measure-gameplay">Measure gameplay · 10 seconds</button><p>Closes this panel while you play. Pause, menus or leaving the tab cancel the run. Starting a measurement also reads the browser’s available renderer name and drawing-buffer size locally. Nothing is uploaded or saved to disk.</p><section id="gameplay-result" hidden aria-label="Saved gameplay sample"><h3>Saved gameplay sample</h3><button id="copy-gameplay-report">Copy this sample</button><p id="copy-gameplay-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><label id="gameplay-report-label" for="gameplay-report-text" hidden>Local report text. Share only if you choose.</label><textarea id="gameplay-report-text" readonly hidden rows="8" style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box" aria-label="Copyable local gameplay report"></textarea><p id="gameplay-result-summary"></p><p id="gameplay-result-readout"></p></section><button id="refresh-speed">Refresh measured speed</button><details id="performance-details"><summary>Performance details · local only</summary><p id="performance-readout">Open while a planet is running to measure.</p><p>Last block of up to 60 frames. P95 is the 95th-percentile frame interval; max and the &gt;50 ms count catch rarer stalls. Physics is per active frame, not tick. Render is elapsed call time, including driver waits, not GPU time. These are not touch-latency measurements. Nothing is uploaded; closing stops measurement.</p></details></dialog><dialog id="god-sheet" aria-labelledby="god-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="god-title">God tools · optional assistance</h2><button id="close-god">Close</button></div><p>Optional assisted actions, not natural evolution. Founders use real resources and suitable habitat; choosing genetics does not guarantee survival. Water and terrain tools deliberately change the environment.</p><section id="assisted-founders"><h3>Land starter · assisted life</h3><p>Select a patch → Preview land starter → Plant. Uses existing resources and suitable moist habitat; does not supply water. Lasting land life is not guaranteed.</p><label for="rooted-founder-variant">Assisted rooted founder</label><select id="rooted-founder-variant" aria-describedby="rooted-founder-choice"><option value="standard" selected>Standard · structure 0%</option><option value="hardy">Hardy · structure 50%</option></select><p id="rooted-founder-choice">Better survival in shallow cold/dry conditions, slower growth and extra wet-habitat costs. Not frost-proof. Same paid body cost. Chosen founder genetics, not evolved adaptation.</p><button id="rooted-founder-open">Preview land starter…</button><p id="rooted-founder-help">Pause and select a patch. <b>Preview land starter…</b> previews its water support before you confirm; Cancel plants nothing.<br>If root water is missing, try <b>Water +</b> on that patch, run the simulation or use Advance, then pause and preview again. Soil needs time to take up water; rain and drying vary.<br>Choose Standard or Hardy, then confirm only when you are ready. Water support is a current check, not a survival promise.</p><p id="rooted-founder-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><button id="combined-pioneer" disabled>Plant paid Pioneer here · 50% aerial allocation</button><button id="combined-pioneer-batch" disabled>Plan Pioneer Auto-seed…</button></section><p id="god-target">Select a patch first.</p><p id="god-availability" role="status" aria-live="polite" style="white-space:pre-line"></p><div id="god-actions"><button id="god-wave">Send wave</button><button id="god-heat">Strike lightning</button><button id="god-scorch" disabled>Scorch · Sandbox</button><button id="god-ignite" disabled>Ignite detritus · Origin</button></div><button id="find-detritus">Find dead organic matter</button><button id="cancel-detritus" hidden>Cancel search</button><button id="god-refresh">Refresh target</button><p id="god-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><details id="transport-section"><summary>Move an existing colony · Origin</summary><p>Pause first, then refresh. Choose a whole colony and a neighboring patch without precise globe taps. No copy, new life or survival guarantee. This is a deliberate god tool, not natural dispersal.</p><button id="transport-pause-path">Close tools to use Pause</button><button id="transport-refresh">Refresh transport options</button><div id="transport-source-step"><h3>1 · Existing colony</h3><div id="transport-sources"></div></div><button id="transport-change-source" hidden>Change source</button><div id="transport-target-step" hidden><h3>2 · Actual neighbor</h3><div id="transport-neighbors"></div></div><button id="transport-change-target" hidden>Change destination</button><button id="transport-prepare" disabled>Review whole-colony move</button><p id="transport-preview"></p><button id="transport-execute" hidden>Move whole colony · remove from source</button><button id="transport-cancel">Cancel plan</button><p id="transport-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="transport-receipt" hidden></p><button id="transport-inspect" hidden>Inspect destination colony</button></details><details id="ignition-ledger" hidden><summary>Last ignition this session · not saved history</summary><p>Fuel heat is calibrated at 30 MJ per kg carbon for gameplay, not measured fuel chemistry. This record is local runtime evidence, not a saved event history, and may be from another planet opened this session.</p><p id="ignition-summary"></p><pre id="ignition-receipt" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></pre></details><details id="god-help"><summary>How these tools work</summary><p>Wave pushes existing water into up to six neighboring patches: at most 25% of this patch’s water, capped at 1 m equivalent. No water creation or terrain erosion.</p><p>Lightning adds a local heat impulse of up to 40°C (capped at 500 K). This is an external god power, not a full lightning simulation. Life responds through actual temperature and flooding rules over time, not guaranteed destruction.</p><p>Scorch destroys 75% of dry Sandbox cover and adds up to 40°C. It can kill rabbits through existing heat limits. This is external destruction, not fire chemistry; no guaranteed recovery.</p><p>Origin only: ignite exposed dead carbon on a completely dry patch. This one-shot oxidation consumes existing detritus and oxygen, adds carbon dioxide and heat, and stops at its fuel, oxygen or temperature limit. It does not directly burn living colonies, spread wildfire or unlock fire-adapted life. Heat can affect life afterward. Wet ground cannot ignite. Use Find dead organic matter to navigate to existing fuel (dry eligible patches are preferred), then inspect Life snapshot. Wet fuel remains wet; use Water − if you deliberately want to expose it. Pause to hold conditions, then reopen or refresh this panel: water can return while time runs. Nothing is automatically drained or seeded, and ignition does not promise a benefit.</p></details></dialog><dialog id="life-sheet" aria-labelledby="life-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="life-title">Life in this patch</h2><button id="close-life">Close</button></div><p id="life-summary" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="wetlands-readout" style="white-space:pre-line"></p><p id="life-habitat"></p><button id="watch-patch">Watch this patch · 10 seconds</button><p class="life-note">Observe actual activity; does not unpause or change speed.</p><div id="fine-water" hidden><p>Selected patch water · fine adjustment. Time keeps running unless paused.</p><button id="water-minus">−0.1 m water</button> <button id="water-plus">+0.1 m water</button><details id="advanced-water"><summary>Set depth or shape basin</summary><div id="target-water" hidden><p>Set this patch to an explicit depth. This supplies or removes water once, not automatic care.</p><label for="water-target">Target depth (metres, 0–5)</label><input id="water-target" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" max="5" step="any" value="0.5"><button id="water-target-apply">Set depth</button> <button id="water-shallow">Set 0.5 m</button><button id="make-pond">Preview basin + water</button><p>Shapes up to 19 terrain patches: a level floor and dry rim raised at least 17 m above it. Supplies 15 m water to the floor and drains the rim once. Existing life is not replaced; changed terrain/water can affect it. No automatic refill.</p></div></details><p id="water-feedback" aria-live="polite"></p><button id="watch-water-change" hidden>Watch this patch</button><p id="watch-water-note" hidden>Observation starts when you click, after the edit. Later changes do not establish a cause.</p></div><button id="refresh-life">Refresh snapshot</button><section aria-label="Current colony shares"><h3>Who lives here</h3><p id="life-colony-shares"></p><p class="life-note">Current biomass shares, not winners or growth rates.</p><div id="offspring-controls" hidden><label for="offspring-parent">Choose a living parent</label><select id="offspring-parent" style="width:100%;min-height:44px"></select><button id="find-offspring" style="min-height:44px">Find living offspring</button><button id="cancel-offspring" hidden>Cancel search</button><p class="life-note">Direct children still alive, anywhere on this planet. Does not change life, pause or speed.</p></div><p id="offspring-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></section><details id="competition-details"><summary>Competition and living traits</summary><section id="competition-panel" hidden aria-labelledby="competition-title"><h3 id="competition-title">Competition at a glance</h3><p id="life-competition" style="white-space:pre-line"></p></section><section id="living-traits" hidden aria-label="Living traits"><b>Living traits · current colonies</b><p id="living-traits-copy"></p><p class="life-note">Potential comes from inherited structure plus living support. Compatibility is not measured photosynthesis or a growth guarantee; dry land is not supported. Biomass trend is reported separately.</p></section></details><details id="cohort-details"><summary>Colony ancestry and detailed traits</summary><div id="life-cohorts"></div></details><details id="condition-details"><summary>Resources and habitat details</summary><p id="life-conditions"></p></details><details id="feeding-details"><summary>Find recorded feeding</summary><button id="find-feeding">Find recorded feeding</button><button id="cancel-feeding" hidden>Cancel search</button><p id="feeding-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="life-note">Amber bands mark patches where at least half the living biomass belongs to colonies with recorded feeding. Amber rings mark mixed patches with some recorded feeding. These are history schematics, not animals or eating animations; producer shapes still show tissue forms. A visible selected patch gets drawing priority and a larger glyph at globe distance.</p></details><details id="life-help"><summary>How to read this ecosystem</summary><p id="life-glossary" class="life-note"></p><p class="life-note">Colony IDs are serial identifiers, not a count of living colonies or species. Births since start includes colonies that later died. Generation counts descent steps from a seeded ancestor. Parent IDs may refer to colonies no longer alive. Net change includes births, losses, movement and interventions.</p><p class="life-note">Watch reports actual photosynthesis, grazing and biological carbon returned to air. The return excludes movement respiration and god tools; this is not a complete carbon budget.</p></details></dialog><section id="guide" hidden><button id="close-guide">Close</button><h2 id="guide-heading">Sandbox habitat guide</h2><div id="goal-card" aria-live="polite"><h3 id="goal-title">Start a habitat</h3><p id="goal-text">Start the game, then check your habitat for a suggested next step.</p></div><div class="guide-actions"><button id="check-habitat">Check habitat</button><button id="guide-land">Find land</button><button id="repeat-guide">First steps</button></div><p><span id="mode-explanation">This sandbox starts with plants and rabbits. It does not yet evolve simple life into new plant or animal groups. Suggestions reflect the current planet, not required levels or guaranteed survival.</span></p><details id="manual"><summary>Controls and field notes</summary><div id="origin-fields" hidden><p>Turquoise mats mark real microbial biomass. Tap <b>Habitat</b> to find shallow water; <b>Seed</b> introduces an existing colony. <b>Nutr. +</b> is a deliberate external nutrient input, not food created by the ecosystem.</p><p>Simple seeds need 0.2–50 m water above 0°C, usable light and resources. Evolved producers with actual paid support and inherited structure can exploit thinner liquid films; the 15–20 cm transition also permits partial aquatic growth. No photosynthesis occurs when dry or frozen. Grazing and movement still require aquatic conditions. Inspect shows carbon biomass, nutrients and the dominant living colony. Descendants can develop aquatic producer forms: cushion, rosette, ribbon, branching and canopy. Shapes follow inherited traits and actual support tissue; these are not terrestrial plant species or animals.</p><p><b>Habitat care:</b> Use <b>Find habitat → Shape nursery → Seed colony → Watch life</b> for a shallow starting patch. Sunlit nursery shapes a 5 m center and neighboring shelf; optional Deep nursery keeps 15 m neighbors. Both have a dry rim and supply water once, not new organisms. Press Play if paused. The older level 15 m basin is still available in Life snapshot. Inspect shallow patches as water changes. For routine replenishment, a <b>Water +</b> tap adds 1 m to the selected patch. <b>Water −</b> removes up to 1 m per tap from only the selected patch, or 5 m per second while painting; it never drains neighbors. Both water brushes are external interventions, not rainfall or evaporation. For precision, open <b>Life snapshot</b> and choose <b>Set 0.5 m</b>. Both supply water once: there is no automatic refill or guaranteed evolution.</p></div><div id="sandbox-fields"><p><b>Read the map:</b> tan is bare land, blue is water, green is vegetation, and orange dots mark living rabbits. Close-up sprouts show real vegetated patches, not individual plant counts; they grow with coverage and shrink when grazed. Rabbit models stand on the surface when you zoom close.</p><p><b>1. Find your land.</b> Tap <b>Land</b> below the game to jump to dry ground. Use <b>＋</b> to get close and <b>Globe</b> to return to a whole-planet view.</p><p><b>2. Shape a habitat.</b> Use Land +/− and Water +/−. Dry land supports rabbits; deep water does not. Pause while sculpting. Water − removes up to 1 m per tap from the selected patch only (5 m per second held), never neighboring water. Water and land brushes respond to how long you hold, not simulation speed. Inspect shows water depth.</p><p><b>3. Plant the land.</b> Choose Plants and paint patches of vegetation. Rabbits eat it, so establish food before adding animals. Sparse food takes longer to graze, but plants can still be lost; regrowth and coexistence are not guaranteed. The Bites counter records positive feeding events, not full meals or food quantity.</p><p><b>4. Add rabbits.</b> Choose Rabbits, then tap suitable land. Watch the population and inspect the surface temperature. This prototype currently has vegetation and rabbits, not a full multi-species ecosystem.</p></div><p><b>Always daylight</b> keeps the side you are viewing lit while the climate simulation continues. You can change the view in the planet menu.</p><p>Use the bottom dock. God opens deliberate tools; choose a brush, then touch the planet. Explore cancels the brush.</p><p><b>Pinch with two fingers</b> to zoom smoothly. In <b>Navigate</b> mode, drag one finger to explore and tap to use a menu or selected tool. Switch to <b>Paint</b> to brush plants or terrain by dragging. Pinching never finishes as a tool tap. Zoom +/− also works.</p><p>Landscape gives you more room. Full screen hides the browser bars. The game automatically resizes when you rotate.</p><p><b>World → Save / Load:</b> Save keeps one planet in this browser on this device, including its ecosystem. It is not a cloud backup. Wait for the Saved message before closing. Clearing site data or using a private browsing session can remove it. Load replaces your unsaved world.</p><p><b>Mobile detail:</b> New browser planets use a lighter grid for smoother play and smaller saves. Existing saved worlds keep their original grid detail when loaded.</p><p>Pause, speed and world controls are in the bottom dock. Open <b>Speed</b> to choose a target of 1, 6 or 24 simulated hours per real second. The top pace button also cycles these targets. Achieved speed is measured separately and may be lower on your device. New worlds start with the 6-hour target; saved worlds keep their requested pace. Pause to sculpt or inspect. Faster time also dries water faster, so watch your habitat.</p></details><a href="qa.html">Executed gameplay tests</a> · <a href="source.html">GPL source</a> · <a href="LICENSE">License</a></section><aside id="gameplay-measure-status" hidden aria-live="polite"><span id="gameplay-measure-message"></span><button id="cancel-gameplay-measure">Cancel</button></aside><dialog id="advance-day-overlay" aria-labelledby="advance-day-title" style="position:fixed;inset:0;margin:0;width:100vw;height:100dvh;max-width:none;max-height:none;box-sizing:border-box;background:#102c30;color:#ecf7f4;border:0;padding:24px"><h2 id="advance-day-title">Advancing your Origin world</h2><p id="advance-day-progress" role="status" aria-live="polite" style="line-height:1.6"></p><p id="advance-day-note">The globe is hidden. Completed simulation progress is kept, including after cancellation. Wait for the final redraw before returning.</p><button id="advance-day-cancel" style="min-height:48px">Cancel further steps</button><button id="advance-day-dismiss" hidden style="min-height:48px">Return to planet</button><section id="advance-day-recovery" hidden><p>Reload discards progress that has not been saved. Graphics cannot safely resume in this page.</p><button id="advance-day-recovery-save" hidden style="min-height:48px">Save completed progress</button><p id="advance-day-recovery-result" role="status"></p><button id="advance-day-reload" style="min-height:48px">Reload game…</button></section></dialog></main><script src="copy-report.js"></script><script src="renderer-info.js"></script><script src="gameplay-measure.js"></script><script src="touch-controls.js"></script><style>#world-library select{min-height:44px;font:inherit;width:100%;max-width:100%;background:#102c30;color:#f4fff8}#world-library{position:static;bottom:auto}#world-library:not([open]){display:block}#rooted-founder-variant{min-height:44px;font:inherit;width:100%;max-width:100%;min-width:0;box-sizing:border-box;background:#102c30;color:#f4fff8;border:1px solid #8aada6;border-radius:6px}#combined-disclosure{position:static;bottom:auto;max-width:100%;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#combined-disclosure:not([open]){display:block}#recovery-backup{min-height:44px;font:inherit;width:100%;max-width:100%;min-width:0;box-sizing:border-box;background:#102c30;color:#f4fff8}#backup-recovery{position:static;bottom:auto;max-width:100%;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#backup-recovery:not([open]){display:block}</style><script src="combined-recovery.js"></script><script src="world-library.js"></script><script src="combined-traits.js"></script><script src="protective-inspection.js"></script><script src="combined-world.js"></script><script src="wetlands-preview.js"></script><script src="rooted-founder.js"></script><script src="stella-storage.js"></script><script src="life-trend.js"></script><script src="patch-watch.js"></script><script src="colony-watch-details.js"></script><script src="colony-transport.js"></script><script src="habitat-plan.js"></script><script src="auto-seed.js"></script><script src="world-ecology.js"></script><script src="sandbox-defense.js"></script><script src="offspring-search.js"></script><script src="advance-day.js"></script><script>
+<aside id="patch-watch-hud" hidden style="position:fixed;left:8px;right:8px;top:60px;z-index:30;background:#102c30ee;padding:10px;border-radius:10px;max-width:520px;max-height:65vh;overflow:auto"><p id="patch-watch-readout" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><details id="patch-watch-colonies" hidden><summary>Individual colony changes</summary><p id="patch-watch-colony-readout" style="white-space:pre-line;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></p></details><button id="cancel-patch-watch">Stop / dismiss observation</button></aside><aside id="welcome-tip" hidden aria-label="Getting started"><p><b>Start a living planet.</b> Find water, seed simple aquatic life, then watch its descendants. World opens your saved planets; God tools are optional assistance. Pinch to zoom; drag to explore.</p><div class="tip-actions"><button id="start-guide">Show me how</button><button id="dismiss-guide">Not now</button></div></aside><dialog id="habitat-sheet" aria-labelledby="habitat-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="habitat-title">Preview habitat changes</h2><button id="habitat-close">Close / cancel</button></div><div class="sheet-actions"><button id="habitat-sunlit" style="min-height:44px">Preview Sunlit · 5 m shelf</button><button id="habitat-deep" style="min-height:44px">Preview Deep · 15 m shelf</button></div><p>Sunlit keeps the center and neighboring floor at 5 m for more light, with less stored water. Deep keeps a 5 m center and 15 m neighbors. Neither guarantees growth; seeding is a separate action.</p><p id="habitat-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="habitat-preview" hidden style="white-space:pre-line;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></p><p id="habitat-warning" hidden><strong>The rim will be raised and dried.</strong> Existing colonies on the rim may lose their habitat; floor colonies may also fare worse. This adds/removes water and changes terrain once, not life, nutrients or a permanent water supply.</p><button id="habitat-apply" hidden style="min-height:44px;width:100%">Apply this plan once</button><p id="habitat-receipt" hidden></p><p>Requires a paused Origin world. To pause, close this panel and use Play / Pause in the bottom dock, then request a fresh preview. Opening or closing this preview never pauses or resumes time.</p></dialog><dialog id="auto-seed-sheet" aria-labelledby="auto-seed-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="auto-seed-title">Auto-seed world</h2><button id="auto-seed-close">Close / cancel</button></div><p>Plan one seed at every eligible seed point on this planet at the moment the plan starts, including offscreen points. There is no visible-marker limit. This uses existing resources and free colony slots; it does not refill nutrients or water.</p><p id="auto-seed-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><button id="auto-seed-apply" hidden>Apply all planned seeds once</button><p>Requires paused Origin. Nothing changes until Apply. Cancel discards the plan. Seeding is a deliberate intervention, not natural birth or a guarantee of survival.</p></dialog><dialog id="more-menu" aria-labelledby="more-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="more-title">Planet tools</h2><button id="close-more" aria-label="Close planet tools">Close</button></div><nav hidden id="menu-groups" aria-label="Tool groups"><button id="menu-plant" aria-controls="group-plant" aria-pressed="true">Plant</button><button id="menu-observe" aria-controls="group-observe" aria-pressed="false">Observe</button><button id="menu-god" aria-controls="group-god" aria-pressed="false">God tools</button><button id="menu-world" aria-controls="group-world" aria-pressed="false">World</button><button id="menu-speed" aria-controls="group-speed" aria-pressed="false">Speed</button></nav><section id="group-plant" aria-label="Plant"><h3>Plant</h3><details id="origin-starter" hidden open><summary id="starter-summary">Start life · shape, seed, inspect</summary><div id="starter-actions"><button id="starter-find">Find habitat</button><button id="starter-basin" title="Shapes up to 19 patches: a 5 m nursery center and neighboring shelf, with a dry rim. Adds water once, not life.">Sunlit nursery</button><button id="starter-seed">Seed colony</button><button id="seed-targets-toggle" aria-pressed="true" title="Show or hide green planting circles and + targets only. Living colonies stay visible; arrival/loss effects have their own control.">Hide seed targets</button></div><p id="starter-info" role="status" aria-live="polite">Find habitat, optionally shape a shallow nursery, then Seed colony and Watch life. Nursery changes terrain and supplies water once, not life.</p></details><div id="origin-auto-seed" hidden><button id="auto-seed-open" disabled>Auto-seed world…</button><p>Review every currently eligible seed point before applying. Planning temporarily uses extra memory; save beforehand on large worlds. No ongoing automatic seeding.</p></div><section id="sandbox-defense-panel" hidden><h3>Inherited plant defenses</h3><button id="defense-land">Find land</button><p id="defense-policy">Optional: enable rare inherited defense variation in future offspring worldwide. Tough plants grow and spread slower and take longer to graze. Existing plants stay unchanged. Save first to restore the earlier rules.</p><button id="defense-enable">Enable inherited defenses</button><div id="defense-choices" hidden><button id="defense-tender">Plant tender</button><button id="defense-tough">Plant tough</button><button id="defense-cancel">Cancel planting</button><p>Tap an empty dry or shallow patch (up to 0.5 m water). Adds a founder with 35% cover; not natural evolution. Existing plants are retained. Toughness does not guarantee survival.</p></div><p id="defense-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></section><button id="help-toggle">Sandbox guide</button></section><section id="group-observe" aria-label="Observe" hidden><h3>Observe</h3><details id="world-ecology-panel" open><summary>Worldwide life · recent events</summary><button id="refresh-world-ecology">Refresh community sample</button><p id="world-ecology-readout" role="status" style="white-space:pre-line;overflow-wrap:anywhere">Open to sample current life and observed recent events.</p><div id="world-form-actions" aria-label="Visit a sampled living growth form"></div></details><div class="sheet-actions"><button id="find-life">Find existing life</button><button id="find-plants" hidden>Find plants</button><button id="find-rabbits" hidden>Find rabbits</button><button id="fit-life">Fit nearby life</button><button id="life-toggle">Life snapshot</button><button id="starter-watch">Watch life</button><button id="starter-inspect">Inspect</button><button id="arrival-effects-toggle" aria-pressed="true" title="Show or hide cyan arrival and amber tracked-loss effects. Does not hide living colonies or green seed hints, or stop event tracking.">Hide arrival/loss effects</button></div></section><section id="group-god" aria-label="God tools" hidden><h3>God tools</h3><p>Deliberate terrain, water, fire and colony interventions. Existing life can be harmed.</p><button id="god-toggle">Show God tools</button></section><section id="group-world" aria-label="World" hidden><h3>World</h3><button id="continue-world">Continue open world</button><p>New living planets include finite soil, wind dispersal and evolving cold/heat protection. Opening older saves keeps their original rules.</p><details id="world-library"><summary>Open a saved planet</summary><p>Start Play, then pause before opening a save. Starting the game does not save over your planet. Choose a save explicitly; originals remain unchanged. Multiple histories are never merged.</p><label for="world-library-source">Save history</label><select id="world-library-source"><option value="current">Saved planets</option><option value="main">Earlier main game</option><option value="wind">Earlier Wind worlds</option></select><button id="world-library-refresh">Find saved planets</button><label for="world-library-entry">Planet</label><select id="world-library-entry"></select><button id="world-library-import" disabled>Open selected planet…</button><button id="world-library-download" disabled>Download a copy</button><button id="world-library-cancel">Cancel selection</button><p id="world-library-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></details><details id="backup-recovery"><summary>Recovery backups</summary><p>Pause the world before restoring. Backups stay in this browser. Download a copy for safekeeping. Restore replaces only the open world after preserving it in a verified recovery checkpoint; the normal saved slot stays unchanged until you choose Save.</p><button id="recovery-refresh">Find saved backups</button><label for="recovery-backup">Verified backup</label><select id="recovery-backup"><option value="">Find backups first</option></select><button id="recovery-download" disabled>Download selected backup</button><button id="recovery-restore" disabled>Restore selected backup…</button><p id="recovery-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></details><button id="combined-new">Save + new living planet…</button><button id="combined-refresh">Refresh world details</button><p id="combined-status" role="status"></p><details id="combined-disclosure"><summary>How this world evolves</summary><p>New worlds begin with simple life. Roots, wind dispersal and cold/heat protection are inherited strategies with costs, not guaranteed land establishment. Evolving protection adds simulation work and may run slower. Older loaded worlds keep their saved rules.</p></details><div class="sheet-actions"><button id="save-world" disabled>Save planet</button><button id="load-world" disabled>Load planet</button><button id="land">Land</button><button id="fullscreen">Full screen</button></div><p>Save stays in this browser on this device. Before replacing an older save, this build preserves one exact pre-upgrade backup here. No cloud backup. Use Recovery backups in this panel to download or restore verified local checkpoints.</p></section><section id="group-speed" aria-label="Speed" hidden><h3>Speed</h3><p>Pause, requested speed, measured speed and bounded one-day advance.</p><button id="speed-toggle">Speed / fast-forward</button><button id="starter-speed">Fast-forward</button></section><p id="release-label">Stella Dei · evolving worlds</p></dialog><dialog id="speed-sheet" aria-labelledby="speed-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="speed-title">Simulation speed</h2><button id="close-speed">Close</button></div><p>Choose a target. Changing speed never unpauses your world.</p><div class="sheet-actions"><button id="speed-slow" aria-pressed="false">Slow · 1 hour / sec</button><button id="speed-grow" aria-pressed="false">Grow · 6 hours / sec</button><button id="speed-fast" aria-pressed="false">Fast-forward · 24 hours / sec</button></div><p id="speed-readout">Start a planet first.</p><p id="speed-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p>Target is your requested speed; Measured is what your device achieves. Simulation steps stay bounded. Time spent in the background is not caught up.</p><section aria-label="3D scene resolution"><h3>3D scene resolution</h3><div class="sheet-actions"><button id="scene-sharp" aria-pressed="false">Sharp · 100%</button><button id="scene-reduced" aria-pressed="false">Reduced · 75%</button><button id="scene-low" aria-pressed="false">Low · 50%</button></div><p id="scene-resolution-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p>Lower resolution makes the 3D planet softer and can reduce rendering work. Controls stay full resolution; simulation detail, time and saves are unchanged. Sharp is the default. This choice resets on page reload.</p></section><section><h3>Advance while paused · Origin</h3><button id="advance-day-start">Advance one day · hide globe</button><p>Pause your Origin world first. Runs 60 bounded simulation steps without drawing the globe between steps. This changes your world; Cancel keeps completed progress. Requested speed and saves are unchanged. No fixed completion time is promised.</p><p id="advance-day-error" role="status"></p></section><button id="measure-gameplay">Measure gameplay · 10 seconds</button><p>Closes this panel while you play. Pause, menus or leaving the tab cancel the run. Starting a measurement also reads the browser’s available renderer name and drawing-buffer size locally. Nothing is uploaded or saved to disk.</p><section id="gameplay-result" hidden aria-label="Saved gameplay sample"><h3>Saved gameplay sample</h3><button id="copy-gameplay-report">Copy this sample</button><p id="copy-gameplay-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><label id="gameplay-report-label" for="gameplay-report-text" hidden>Local report text. Share only if you choose.</label><textarea id="gameplay-report-text" readonly hidden rows="8" style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box" aria-label="Copyable local gameplay report"></textarea><p id="gameplay-result-summary"></p><p id="gameplay-result-readout"></p></section><button id="refresh-speed">Refresh measured speed</button><details id="performance-details"><summary>Performance details · local only</summary><p id="performance-readout">Open while a planet is running to measure.</p><p>Last block of up to 60 frames. P95 is the 95th-percentile frame interval; max and the &gt;50 ms count catch rarer stalls. Physics is per active frame, not tick. Render is elapsed call time, including driver waits, not GPU time. These are not touch-latency measurements. Nothing is uploaded; closing stops measurement.</p></details></dialog><dialog id="god-sheet" aria-labelledby="god-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="god-title">God tools · optional assistance</h2><button id="close-god">Close</button></div><p>Optional assisted actions, not natural evolution. Founders use real resources and suitable habitat; choosing genetics does not guarantee survival. Water and terrain tools deliberately change the environment.</p><section id="assisted-founders"><h3>Land starter · assisted life</h3><p>Select a patch → Preview land starter → Plant. Uses existing resources and suitable moist habitat; does not supply water. Lasting land life is not guaranteed.</p><label for="rooted-founder-variant">Assisted rooted founder</label><select id="rooted-founder-variant" aria-describedby="rooted-founder-choice"><option value="standard" selected>Standard · structure 0%</option><option value="hardy">Hardy · structure 50%</option></select><p id="rooted-founder-choice">Better survival in shallow cold/dry conditions, slower growth and extra wet-habitat costs. Not frost-proof. Same paid body cost. Chosen founder genetics, not evolved adaptation.</p><button id="rooted-founder-open">Preview land starter…</button><p id="rooted-founder-help">Pause and select a patch. <b>Preview land starter…</b> previews its water support before you confirm; Cancel plants nothing.<br>If root water is missing, try <b>Water +</b> on that patch, run the simulation or use Advance, then pause and preview again. Soil needs time to take up water; rain and drying vary.<br>Choose Standard or Hardy, then confirm only when you are ready. Water support is a current check, not a survival promise.</p><button id="rooted-founder-view" hidden>View planted colony</button><p id="rooted-founder-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><button id="combined-pioneer" disabled>Plant paid Pioneer here · 50% aerial allocation</button><button id="combined-pioneer-batch" disabled>Plan Pioneer Auto-seed…</button></section><p id="god-target">Select a patch first.</p><p id="god-availability" role="status" aria-live="polite" style="white-space:pre-line"></p><div id="god-actions"><button id="god-wave">Send wave</button><button id="god-heat">Strike lightning</button><button id="god-scorch" disabled>Scorch · Sandbox</button><button id="god-ignite" disabled>Ignite detritus · Origin</button></div><button id="find-detritus">Find dead organic matter</button><button id="cancel-detritus" hidden>Cancel search</button><button id="god-refresh">Refresh target</button><p id="god-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><details id="transport-section"><summary>Move an existing colony · Origin</summary><p>Pause first, then refresh. Choose a whole colony and a neighboring patch without precise globe taps. No copy, new life or survival guarantee. This is a deliberate god tool, not natural dispersal.</p><button id="transport-pause-path">Close tools to use Pause</button><button id="transport-refresh">Refresh transport options</button><div id="transport-source-step"><h3>1 · Existing colony</h3><div id="transport-sources"></div></div><button id="transport-change-source" hidden>Change source</button><div id="transport-target-step" hidden><h3>2 · Actual neighbor</h3><div id="transport-neighbors"></div></div><button id="transport-change-target" hidden>Change destination</button><button id="transport-prepare" disabled>Review whole-colony move</button><p id="transport-preview"></p><button id="transport-execute" hidden>Move whole colony · remove from source</button><button id="transport-cancel">Cancel plan</button><p id="transport-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="transport-receipt" hidden></p><button id="transport-inspect" hidden>Inspect destination colony</button></details><details id="ignition-ledger" hidden><summary>Last ignition this session · not saved history</summary><p>Fuel heat is calibrated at 30 MJ per kg carbon for gameplay, not measured fuel chemistry. This record is local runtime evidence, not a saved event history, and may be from another planet opened this session.</p><p id="ignition-summary"></p><pre id="ignition-receipt" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></pre></details><details id="god-help"><summary>How these tools work</summary><p>Wave pushes existing water into up to six neighboring patches: at most 25% of this patch’s water, capped at 1 m equivalent. No water creation or terrain erosion.</p><p>Lightning adds a local heat impulse of up to 40°C (capped at 500 K). This is an external god power, not a full lightning simulation. Life responds through actual temperature and flooding rules over time, not guaranteed destruction.</p><p>Scorch destroys 75% of dry Sandbox cover and adds up to 40°C. It can kill rabbits through existing heat limits. This is external destruction, not fire chemistry; no guaranteed recovery.</p><p>Origin only: ignite exposed dead carbon on a completely dry patch. This one-shot oxidation consumes existing detritus and oxygen, adds carbon dioxide and heat, and stops at its fuel, oxygen or temperature limit. It does not directly burn living colonies, spread wildfire or unlock fire-adapted life. Heat can affect life afterward. Wet ground cannot ignite. Use Find dead organic matter to navigate to existing fuel (dry eligible patches are preferred), then inspect Life snapshot. Wet fuel remains wet; use Water − if you deliberately want to expose it. Pause to hold conditions, then reopen or refresh this panel: water can return while time runs. Nothing is automatically drained or seeded, and ignition does not promise a benefit.</p></details></dialog><dialog id="life-sheet" aria-labelledby="life-title"><div class="sheet-heading"><h2 id="life-title">Life in this patch</h2><button id="close-life">Close</button></div><p id="life-summary" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="wetlands-readout" style="white-space:pre-line"></p><p id="life-habitat"></p><button id="watch-patch">Watch this patch · 10 seconds</button><p class="life-note">Observe actual activity; does not unpause or change speed.</p><div id="fine-water" hidden><p>Selected patch water · fine adjustment. Time keeps running unless paused.</p><button id="water-minus">−0.1 m water</button> <button id="water-plus">+0.1 m water</button><details id="advanced-water"><summary>Set depth or shape basin</summary><div id="target-water" hidden><p>Set this patch to an explicit depth. This supplies or removes water once, not automatic care.</p><label for="water-target">Target depth (metres, 0–5)</label><input id="water-target" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" max="5" step="any" value="0.5"><button id="water-target-apply">Set depth</button> <button id="water-shallow">Set 0.5 m</button><button id="make-pond">Preview basin + water</button><p>Shapes up to 19 terrain patches: a level floor and dry rim raised at least 17 m above it. Supplies 15 m water to the floor and drains the rim once. Existing life is not replaced; changed terrain/water can affect it. No automatic refill.</p></div></details><p id="water-feedback" aria-live="polite"></p><button id="watch-water-change" hidden>Watch this patch</button><p id="watch-water-note" hidden>Observation starts when you click, after the edit. Later changes do not establish a cause.</p></div><button id="refresh-life">Refresh snapshot</button><section aria-label="Current colony shares"><h3>Who lives here</h3><p id="life-colony-shares"></p><p class="life-note">Current biomass shares, not winners or growth rates.</p><div id="offspring-controls" hidden><label for="offspring-parent">Choose a living parent</label><select id="offspring-parent" style="width:100%;min-height:44px"></select><button id="find-offspring" style="min-height:44px">Find living offspring</button><button id="cancel-offspring" hidden>Cancel search</button><p class="life-note">Direct children still alive, anywhere on this planet. Does not change life, pause or speed.</p></div><p id="offspring-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></section><details id="competition-details"><summary>Competition and living traits</summary><section id="competition-panel" hidden aria-labelledby="competition-title"><h3 id="competition-title">Competition at a glance</h3><p id="life-competition" style="white-space:pre-line"></p></section><section id="living-traits" hidden aria-label="Living traits"><b>Living traits · current colonies</b><p id="living-traits-copy"></p><p class="life-note">Potential comes from inherited structure plus living support. Compatibility is not measured photosynthesis or a growth guarantee; dry land is not supported. Biomass trend is reported separately.</p></section></details><details id="cohort-details"><summary>Colony ancestry and detailed traits</summary><div id="life-cohorts"></div></details><details id="condition-details"><summary>Resources and habitat details</summary><p id="life-conditions"></p></details><details id="feeding-details"><summary>Find recorded feeding</summary><button id="find-feeding">Find recorded feeding</button><button id="cancel-feeding" hidden>Cancel search</button><p id="feeding-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="life-note">Amber bands mark patches where at least half the living biomass belongs to colonies with recorded feeding. Amber rings mark mixed patches with some recorded feeding. These are history schematics, not animals or eating animations; producer shapes still show tissue forms. A visible selected patch gets drawing priority and a larger glyph at globe distance.</p></details><details id="life-help"><summary>How to read this ecosystem</summary><p id="life-glossary" class="life-note"></p><p class="life-note">Colony IDs are serial identifiers, not a count of living colonies or species. Births since start includes colonies that later died. Generation counts descent steps from a seeded ancestor. Parent IDs may refer to colonies no longer alive. Net change includes births, losses, movement and interventions.</p><p class="life-note">Watch reports actual photosynthesis, grazing and biological carbon returned to air. The return excludes movement respiration and god tools; this is not a complete carbon budget.</p></details></dialog><section id="guide" hidden><button id="close-guide">Close</button><h2 id="guide-heading">Sandbox habitat guide</h2><div id="goal-card" aria-live="polite"><h3 id="goal-title">Start a habitat</h3><p id="goal-text">Start the game, then check your habitat for a suggested next step.</p></div><div class="guide-actions"><button id="check-habitat">Check habitat</button><button id="guide-land">Find land</button><button id="repeat-guide">First steps</button></div><p><span id="mode-explanation">This sandbox starts with plants and rabbits. It does not yet evolve simple life into new plant or animal groups. Suggestions reflect the current planet, not required levels or guaranteed survival.</span></p><details id="manual"><summary>Controls and field notes</summary><div id="origin-fields" hidden><p>Turquoise mats mark real microbial biomass. Tap <b>Habitat</b> to find shallow water; <b>Seed</b> introduces an existing colony. <b>Nutr. +</b> is a deliberate external nutrient input, not food created by the ecosystem.</p><p>Simple seeds need 0.2–50 m water above 0°C, usable light and resources. Evolved producers with actual paid support and inherited structure can exploit thinner liquid films; the 15–20 cm transition also permits partial aquatic growth. No photosynthesis occurs when dry or frozen. Grazing and movement still require aquatic conditions. Inspect shows carbon biomass, nutrients and the dominant living colony. Descendants can develop aquatic producer forms: cushion, rosette, ribbon, branching and canopy. Shapes follow inherited traits and actual support tissue; these are not terrestrial plant species or animals.</p><p><b>Habitat care:</b> Use <b>Find habitat → Shape nursery → Seed colony → Watch life</b> for a shallow starting patch. Sunlit nursery shapes a 5 m center and neighboring shelf; optional Deep nursery keeps 15 m neighbors. Both have a dry rim and supply water once, not new organisms. Press Play if paused. The older level 15 m basin is still available in Life snapshot. Inspect shallow patches as water changes. For routine replenishment, a <b>Water +</b> tap adds 1 m to the selected patch. <b>Water −</b> removes up to 1 m per tap from only the selected patch, or 5 m per second while painting; it never drains neighbors. Both water brushes are external interventions, not rainfall or evaporation. For precision, open <b>Life snapshot</b> and choose <b>Set 0.5 m</b>. Both supply water once: there is no automatic refill or guaranteed evolution.</p></div><div id="sandbox-fields"><p><b>Read the map:</b> tan is bare land, blue is water, green is vegetation, and orange dots mark living rabbits. Close-up sprouts show real vegetated patches, not individual plant counts; they grow with coverage and shrink when grazed. Rabbit models stand on the surface when you zoom close.</p><p><b>1. Find your land.</b> Tap <b>Land</b> below the game to jump to dry ground. Use <b>＋</b> to get close and <b>Globe</b> to return to a whole-planet view.</p><p><b>2. Shape a habitat.</b> Use Land +/− and Water +/−. Dry land supports rabbits; deep water does not. Pause while sculpting. Water − removes up to 1 m per tap from the selected patch only (5 m per second held), never neighboring water. Water and land brushes respond to how long you hold, not simulation speed. Inspect shows water depth.</p><p><b>3. Plant the land.</b> Choose Plants and paint patches of vegetation. Rabbits eat it, so establish food before adding animals. Sparse food takes longer to graze, but plants can still be lost; regrowth and coexistence are not guaranteed. The Bites counter records positive feeding events, not full meals or food quantity.</p><p><b>4. Add rabbits.</b> Choose Rabbits, then tap suitable land. Watch the population and inspect the surface temperature. This prototype currently has vegetation and rabbits, not a full multi-species ecosystem.</p></div><p><b>Always daylight</b> keeps the side you are viewing lit while the climate simulation continues. You can change the view in the planet menu.</p><p>Use the bottom dock. God opens deliberate tools; choose a brush, then touch the planet. Explore cancels the brush.</p><p><b>Pinch with two fingers</b> to zoom smoothly. In <b>Navigate</b> mode, drag one finger to explore and tap to use a menu or selected tool. Switch to <b>Paint</b> to brush plants or terrain by dragging. Pinching never finishes as a tool tap. Zoom +/− also works.</p><p>Landscape gives you more room. Full screen hides the browser bars. The game automatically resizes when you rotate.</p><p><b>World → Save / Load:</b> Save keeps one planet in this browser on this device, including its ecosystem. It is not a cloud backup. Wait for the Saved message before closing. Clearing site data or using a private browsing session can remove it. Load replaces your unsaved world.</p><p><b>Mobile detail:</b> New browser planets use a lighter grid for smoother play and smaller saves. Existing saved worlds keep their original grid detail when loaded.</p><p>Pause, speed and world controls are in the bottom dock. Open <b>Speed</b> to choose a target of 1, 6 or 24 simulated hours per real second. The top pace button also cycles these targets. Achieved speed is measured separately and may be lower on your device. New worlds start with the 6-hour target; saved worlds keep their requested pace. Pause to sculpt or inspect. Faster time also dries water faster, so watch your habitat.</p></details><a href="qa.html">Executed gameplay tests</a> · <a href="source.html">GPL source</a> · <a href="LICENSE">License</a></section><aside id="gameplay-measure-status" hidden aria-live="polite"><span id="gameplay-measure-message"></span><button id="cancel-gameplay-measure">Cancel</button></aside><dialog id="advance-day-overlay" aria-labelledby="advance-day-title" style="position:fixed;inset:0;margin:0;width:100vw;height:100dvh;max-width:none;max-height:none;box-sizing:border-box;background:#102c30;color:#ecf7f4;border:0;padding:24px"><h2 id="advance-day-title">Advancing your Origin world</h2><p id="advance-day-progress" role="status" aria-live="polite" style="line-height:1.6"></p><p id="advance-day-note">The globe is hidden. Completed simulation progress is kept, including after cancellation. Wait for the final redraw before returning.</p><button id="advance-day-cancel" style="min-height:48px">Cancel further steps</button><button id="advance-day-dismiss" hidden style="min-height:48px">Return to planet</button><section id="advance-day-recovery" hidden><p>Reload discards progress that has not been saved. Graphics cannot safely resume in this page.</p><button id="advance-day-recovery-save" hidden style="min-height:48px">Save completed progress</button><p id="advance-day-recovery-result" role="status"></p><button id="advance-day-reload" style="min-height:48px">Reload game…</button></section></dialog></main><script src="copy-report.js"></script><script src="renderer-info.js"></script><script src="gameplay-measure.js"></script><script src="touch-controls.js"></script><style>#world-library select{min-height:44px;font:inherit;width:100%;max-width:100%;background:#102c30;color:#f4fff8}#world-library{position:static;bottom:auto}#world-library:not([open]){display:block}#rooted-founder-variant{min-height:44px;font:inherit;width:100%;max-width:100%;min-width:0;box-sizing:border-box;background:#102c30;color:#f4fff8;border:1px solid #8aada6;border-radius:6px}#combined-disclosure{position:static;bottom:auto;max-width:100%;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#combined-disclosure:not([open]){display:block}#recovery-backup{min-height:44px;font:inherit;width:100%;max-width:100%;min-width:0;box-sizing:border-box;background:#102c30;color:#f4fff8}#backup-recovery{position:static;bottom:auto;max-width:100%;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#backup-recovery:not([open]){display:block}</style><script src="combined-recovery.js"></script><script src="world-library.js"></script><script src="combined-traits.js"></script><script src="protective-inspection.js"></script><script src="combined-world.js"></script><script src="wetlands-preview.js"></script><script src="rooted-founder.js"></script><script src="stella-storage.js"></script><script src="life-trend.js"></script><script src="patch-watch.js"></script><script src="colony-watch-details.js"></script><script src="colony-trans